@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1125 = private unnamed_addr constant [1940 x i8] c"## What it does\0AIdentifies FastAPI routes with deprecated uses of `Depends` or similar.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe [FastAPI documentation] recommends the use of [`typing.Annotated`][typing-annotated]\0Afor defining route dependencies and parameters, rather than using `Depends`,\0A`Query` or similar as a default value for a parameter. Using this approach\0Aeverywhere helps ensure consistency and clarity in defining dependencies\0Aand parameters.\0A\0A`Annotated` was added to the `typing` module in Python 3.9; however,\0Athe third-party [`typing_extensions`][typing-extensions] package\0Aprovides a backport that can be used on older versions of Python.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI\0A\0Aapp = FastAPI()\0A\0A\0Aasync def common_parameters(q: str | None = None, skip: int = 0, limit: int = 100):\0A    return {\22q\22: q, \22skip\22: skip, \22limit\22: limit}\0A\0A\0A@app.get(\22/items/\22)\0Aasync def read_items(commons: dict = Depends(common_parameters)):\0A    return commons\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import Annotated\0A\0Afrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI\0A\0Aapp = FastAPI()\0A\0A\0Aasync def common_parameters(q: str | None = None, skip: int = 0, limit: int = 100):\0A    return {\22q\22: q, \22skip\22: skip, \22limit\22: limit}\0A\0A\0A@app.get(\22/items/\22)\0Aasync def read_items(commons: Annotated[dict, Depends(common_parameters)]):\0A    return commons\0A```\0A\0A## Availability\0A\0ABecause this rule relies on the third-party `typing_extensions` module for Python versions\0Abefore 3.9, its diagnostic will not be emitted, and no fix will be offered, if\0A`typing_extensions` imports have been disabled by the [`lint.typing-extensions`] linter option.\0A\0A## Options\0A\0A- `lint.typing-extensions`\0A\0A[FastAPI documentation]: https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/query-params-str-validations/?h=annotated#advantages-of-annotated\0A[typing-annotated]: https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Annotated\0A[typing-extensions]: https://typing-extensions.readthedocs.io/en/stable/\0A", align 1
