@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1187 = private unnamed_addr constant [694 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for potential uses of hardcoded passwords in function argument\0Adefaults.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIncluding a hardcoded password in source code is a security risk, as an\0Aattacker could discover the password and use it to gain unauthorized\0Aaccess.\0A\0AInstead, store passwords and other secrets in configuration files,\0Aenvironment variables, or other sources that are excluded from version\0Acontrol.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Adef connect_to_server(password=\22hunter2\22): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport os\0A\0A\0Adef connect_to_server(password=os.environ[\22PASSWORD\22]): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-259](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/259.html)\0A", align 1
