@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1216 = private unnamed_addr constant [588 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `getattr` that take a constant attribute value as an\0Aargument (e.g., `getattr(obj, \22foo\22)`).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`getattr` is used to access attributes dynamically. If the attribute is\0Adefined as a constant, it is no safer than a typical property access. When\0Apossible, prefer property access over `getattr` calls, as the former is\0Amore concise and idiomatic.\0A\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Agetattr(obj, \22foo\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aobj.foo\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `getattr`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#getattr)\0A", align 1
