@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1244 = private unnamed_addr constant [508 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary list or tuple literals.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to use a list or tuple literal within a call to `dict()`.\0AIt can be rewritten as a dict literal (`{}`).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adict([(1, 2), (3, 4)])\0Adict(((1, 2), (3, 4)))\0Adict([])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A{1: 2, 3: 4}\0A{1: 2, 3: 4}\0A{}\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may occasionally drop comments\0Awhen rewriting the call. In most cases, though, comments will be preserved.\0A", align 1
