@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1273 = private unnamed_addr constant [609 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for numeric literals with a string representation longer than ten\0Acharacters.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf a function has a default value where the literal representation is\0Agreater than 10 characters, the value is likely to be an implementation\0Adetail or a constant that varies depending on the system you're running on.\0A\0ADefault values like these should generally be omitted from stubs. Use\0Aellipses (`...`) instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: int = 693568516352839939918568862861217771399698285293568) -> None: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef foo(arg: int = ...) -> None: ...\0A```\0A", align 1
