@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1369 = private unnamed_addr constant [2229 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for undocumented public function definitions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APublic functions should be documented via docstrings to outline their\0Apurpose and behavior.\0A\0AGenerally, a function docstring should describe the function's behavior,\0Aarguments, side effects, exceptions, return values, and any other\0Ainformation that may be relevant to the user.\0A\0AIf the codebase adheres to a standard format for function docstrings, follow\0Athat format for consistency.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0AUse instead (using the NumPy docstring format):\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Parameters\0A    ----------\0A    distance : float\0A        Distance traveled.\0A    time : float\0A        Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns\0A    -------\0A    float\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Raises\0A    ------\0A    FasterThanLightError\0A        If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0AOr, using the Google docstring format:\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Raises:\0A        FasterThanLightError: If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.ignore-decorators`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Style Python Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#s3.8-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
