@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1448 = private unnamed_addr constant [446 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary direct calls to lambda expressions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ACalling a lambda expression directly is unnecessary. The expression can be\0Aexecuted inline instead to improve readability.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aarea = (lambda r: 3.14 * r**2)(radius)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aarea = 3.14 * radius**2\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Lambdas](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/expressions.html#lambda)\0A", align 1
