@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1461 = private unnamed_addr constant [533 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for import aliases that do not rename the original package.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe import alias is redundant and should be removed to avoid confusion.\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis fix is marked as always unsafe because the user may be intentionally\0Are-exporting the import. While statements like `import numpy as numpy`\0Aappear redundant, they can have semantic meaning in certain contexts.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport numpy as numpy\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport numpy as np\0A```\0A\0Aor\0A\0A```python\0Aimport numpy\0A```\0A", align 1
