@anon.8ad231a129453d088979dfad2582f60a.1493 = private unnamed_addr constant [1051 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function calls in dataclass attribute defaults.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFunction calls are only performed once, at definition time. The returned\0Avalue is then reused by all instances of the dataclass. This can lead to\0Aunexpected behavior when the function call returns a mutable object, as\0Achanges to the object will be shared across all instances.\0A\0AIf a field needs to be initialized with a mutable object, use the\0A`field(default_factory=...)` pattern.\0A\0AAttributes whose default arguments are `NewType` calls\0Awhere the original type is immutable are ignored.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass\0A\0A\0Adef simple_list() -> list[int]:\0A    return [1, 2, 3, 4]\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass A:\0A    mutable_default: list[int] = simple_list()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\0A\0A\0Adef creating_list() -> list[int]:\0A    return [1, 2, 3, 4]\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass A:\0A    mutable_default: list[int] = field(default_factory=creating_list)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-bugbear.extend-immutable-calls`\0A", align 1
